277
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:41,240
Open wide.

278
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:53,600
This doesn't look good.

279
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:58,780
Well, it looks like you have a cavity and your crown is loose.

280
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:03,080
We'll need to put in a filling before it gets any worse.

281
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:08,280
And the crown probably needs to be refitted.

282
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:12,760
I'm going to order some x-rays.

283
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:13,260
Is it going to hurt?

284
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:15,930
No, not at all.

285
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:19,450
Just lay back and relax.

286
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:33,680
Okay, spit.

287
00:12:43,460 --> 00:12:51,160
Well, Marco, speaking of dentists, have you ever had an experience like this where you spat out a tooth at the dentist?

288
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:58,360
Well, nothing so serious as this, but actually, recently when I was in Cambodia...

289
00:12:58,360 --> 00:13:01,040
Oh, right, you called us in Cambodia.

290
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:02,040
Yeah.

291
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:04,820
Well, our taxi driver offered us to have some local food.

292
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:09,320
And he said, well, we're going to have a dog.

293
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:10,220
So that was interesting.

294
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:12,900
Actually, it wasn't that bad.

295
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:13,600
It was pretty good.

296
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:16,680
But, you know, if you get around the fact that it's a dog...

297
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:17,800
So what does this have to do with your teeth?

298
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:21,160
I was eating it and I bit a bone that was hidden.

299
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:23,260
And I chipped my tooth.

300
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,920
So you broke part of your tooth.

301
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:28,520
Yeah, like half of it, which I had already chipped before.

302
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:31,080
So I had to go to the dentist.

303
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:35,800
And so the dentist created a new crown, not with gold or porcelain, actually with a paste.

304
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:39,280
And then it becomes hard and it just looks normal.

305
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:43,320
It doesn't even look like I have a fake crown, so to say.

306
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:45,620
But dentists can be really expensive.

307
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:46,780
So how much did this cost?

308
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,740
Well, this was for the bargain price of $10.

309
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,320
$10.

310
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:54,320
$10.

311
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,840
That's how much it cost.

312
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,900
So we should all go to Cambodia for dentistry.

313
00:13:58,260 --> 00:13:59,700
Yeah, because actually it was pretty good.

314
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:01,080
He looked really young, though.

315
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:04,140
I was kind of scared because when he walked in, he looked like he was 19.

316
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,320
But I asked him his age and he was like 30.

317
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:08,740
OK, well, you're very trusting.

318
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:09,860
Yeah.

319
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:13,400
So I imagine that you guys maybe have some dental experiences.

320
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:16,080
So why don't you come to our website and tell us all about it?

321
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:23,780
Yeah, visit us at EnglishPod.com and you can find lots more resources for learning English there.

322
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:27,100
Well, guys, thanks for listening and until next time.

323
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:27,720
Bye.

324
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:36,043
Bye.
